  "worked_solution": "Let $f(t)=50t$ represent the rate at which money enters the account, and let $M(T)$ be the total amount of money in the account after $T$ weeks.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nM(T)=M(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(T) & =M(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =200+{\\int }_{0}^{T}50t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={200+(25{t}^{2})|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =200+25{T}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nM(t)=200+25{t}^{2}.\n$$",
